{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>This day I begin to put your dread.</b> The explanation is: beforehand, when they saw that the seven nations [realized] that Ammon and Edom did not allow Israel passage through their borders, and also Sihon king of Moab refused, the seven nations said: now, if Ammon and Moab — even when each was on its own — Israel could not withstand them, we who are sevenfold all the more, how much more so [that Israel] will not be able to withstand us. Once Sihon and Og fell before Israel, the Canaanites were terrified — this is what is meant by <b>this day I begin to put your dread</b> etc."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:51:26.055345525Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}